From baff3258736b0592f5d8fdf3dfd3777a7e21b1c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 11:27:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(fx): Move FX mute/solo, idle gating, per-set strip reset
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Review fixes for the Move-track strips feature:

- Move FX strip now obeys the channel's mute/solo via a new
  shadow_slot_active_gain() helper (was mixing at raw strip volume, so
  Mute+Track / solo had no effect on a peeled Move track).
- Wire the previously-unused shadow_move_fx_has_fx() in: when no FX is
  loaded, skip the memcpy + FX loop and mix straight from la_cache.
- Relocate the Move FX block ahead of the synth block and relax the synth
  idle gate to (!have_move_track || !route_to_synth) — an idle synth with
  Move>Slot off no longer runs its FX chain on silence, and the idle-continue
  can't skip the (now-earlier) Move FX block. Mixing is additive so order is
  unchanged.
- restoreMoveFxFromFiles applies all strip levels every restore, defaulting
  to unity/no-send when the meta file is absent, so a new set no longer
  inherits the prior set's Move FX levels (shim strips are global, never reset).

(Review finding "drawMasterFxModuleSelect hardcodes master components" was a
false positive — it reads ctx.MASTER_FX_CHAIN_COMPONENTS, a getter returning
activeFxBus.components; the shadow_ui.js:9502 sibling is gated to the master bus.)

