From f9ea099b286ee05a50b5a31221ef3678fa0d4ced Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 11:47:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(fx): keep Move FX strip independent of synth slot
 mute/solo
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Revert the mute/solo coupling from 29e77454. Gating the Move FX strip by the
synth slot's mute/solo recouples exactly what Move>Slot decouples — the whole
point is that the peeled Move track is independent of the synth on the same
channel. The Move FX strip uses its own volume only (set it to 0 to silence;
Move's native track mute still silences the source). Drop the now-unused
shadow_slot_active_gain() helper. The other 29e77454 fixes (idle gating, Move FX
block relocation + relaxed synth idle gate, per-set strip reset) are unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
