Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The home-screen param knobs (71-78) on the FX chain overview were gated to the
master bus only ('master-only for now') — Send A/B and Move FX fell through to
the generic chain-slot knob path, editing Schwung slot 1's synth. Generalize the
buildKnobContextForKnob branch to ANY bus: use activeFxBus.components + each
component's paramPrefix (the param engine's isMasterFx path + getMasterFx*
helpers are already bus-aware via activeFxBus, so only the component list + key
prefixes were pinned to master). Bus-aware overlay title tag too.

Also add activeFxBus.id to the knob-context cache key (cachedKnobContextsFxBus):
now that every bus uses FX-overview contexts, a bus switch with the same
view/slot index must invalidate the cache or knobs leak params across buses.

NOTE: generalization device-verified; the cache-key fix is committed but awaits
device re-verification (Move went unreachable before redeploy).

